    "diagramPlacement": "beside-prompt",
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\overrightarrow{AB}=2(-\\underset{\\sim}{a}+\\underset{\\sim}{b})=2\\overrightarrow{MN}$, so $AB\\parallel MN$.",
      "worked": "Since $M$ and $N$ are midpoints, $\\overrightarrow{OA}=2\\underset{\\sim}{a}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}=2\\underset{\\sim}{b}$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{AB}&=\\overrightarrow{OB}-\\overrightarrow{OA}\\\\&=-2\\underset{\\sim}{a}+2\\underset{\\sim}{b},\\\\\\overrightarrow{MN}&=\\overrightarrow{ON}-\\overrightarrow{OM}\\\\&=-\\underset{\\sim}{a}+\\underset{\\sim}{b},\\\\\\overrightarrow{AB}&=2(-\\underset{\\sim}{a}+\\underset{\\sim}{b})\\\\&=2\\overrightarrow{MN}.\\end{aligned}$$\nTherefore $AB\\parallel MN$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 33
